    <statement><p>Compute the following limit.  If the limit goes to <m>\infty</m> or <m>- \infty</m> enter INFINITY or -INFINITY, respectively.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \lim_{t \to \infty} \left( 12e^{-0.15 t} + 17 \right) =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>17</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



<me>\displaystyle \lim_{t \to \infty} \left( 12e^{-0.15 t} + 17 \right) = 0 + 17 = 17</me>



